  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9f3b10ad4d1f4b6aa84f8f6d5e9a19c0, type: 3}
  m_Name: text_wrath_deep
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::AncientTextData
  textId: wrath_deep
  title: When We Came Apart
  body: "We should tell you the part we are ashamed of, because pride in the archive
    would be its own kind of lie.\n\nThere was a stretch \u2014 after we understood,
    before we accepted \u2014 when we could not stand the sight of one another. Every
    glance was a reminder. The healer stopped meeting our eyes. The strong one picked
    fights she did not want, just to feel something other than the ending. We fought
    the islands and we fought each other, and for a while it was uncertain which
    would finish us first.\n\nWe are not writing to warn you away from this. You
    may not be able to avoid it; we could not. We are writing so that when it happens,
    you will know it is a season and not a verdict. Groups come apart at the exact
    place they are most afraid. The coming-apart is not the failure. Staying apart
    is. We found our way back. It is the only thing we did that we are truly proud
    of. Find your way back too."
